Title: The live region keeps saying indexing is on after the switch goes off
Created: 2026-09-14
Author: claude
Blocked-by: 0769

--- log ---
2026-09-14T12:15Z claude created
2026-09-14T12:16Z claude note Found by ticket 0769's Orca pass, on the author's own desktop with Orca running and speech captured to a debug log. This is the defect that pass existed to find, and no headless test could have: the region is present, correctly built and correctly exposed, and says the wrong thing.

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0686 item (1) added a visually hidden live region, `sdt-announcer`, so a
screen-reader user hears a change of state — scanning, waiting for resources, an
error, indexing switched on or off — once it has held for
`SDT_ANNOUNCE_SETTLE_MS`.

The region is built correctly. Read from OUTSIDE the process over AT-SPI on
2026-09-14 it reports `live: polite`, `atomic: true`,
`container-live-role: status` — exactly what an assistive technology needs.

**It is not rewritten when the indexing switch is turned off.**

## The measurement

Real Zotero 10.0.1, sitter 0.4.10, accessibility bus on, Orca running. The
panel's switch was clicked and the panel read at four points:

| after | `state.phase` | switch label | `sdt-announcer` |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 s | `switched-off` | Turn indexing on | **Indexing is on.** Everything in view is indexed… |
| 3 s | `switched-off` | Turn indexing on | **Indexing is on.** … |
| 6 s | `switched-off` | Turn indexing on | **Indexing is on.** … |
| 10 s | `switched-off` | Turn indexing on | **Indexing is on.** … |

The phase changes within a second and the button's own label follows it. The
region does not move, at five times the settle.

## Why it matters more than a stale string

The sighted user sees the button change. The screen-reader user is *told*, by
the element built for exactly this purpose, that indexing is on while it is off.
A region that is silent would be a gap; a region asserting the opposite state is
worse than not having one, because the reader has no reason to doubt it.

Orca was confirmed to speak the rest of the panel in the same session —
`'Index push button'`, `'Indexing assistant frame'`,
`'Turn indexing off push button'`, `'Library: Ma bibliothèque — 0 files
indexed'` — so this is not Orca failing to read the window.

## Relevant files

- `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` — `announceSDTTransition`, around line 1979:
  the settle logic, `_sdtAnnounced` and `_sdtLeftAt` on the dialog
- `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` — `describeSDTSwitchKind`, around line 1527:
  `phase === 'switched-off'` returns `'off'`, so the kind DOES change
- `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs` — the existing announce scenarios, which pass

## Actions

1. Find why the writer does not run for this transition. The kind changes, so
   the suspects are the render path not reaching `announceSDTTransition` while
   switched off, or a settle that never expires.
2. Fix it so the region carries the state that is true.

## Test

Red first, and the existing suite is the warning: five announce scenarios pass
today while the live window does the wrong thing, so whatever is added must
fail against this build. Drive the real switch-off path rather than calling the
announcer directly — the existing tests establish the settle logic in
isolation, and the isolation is where the defect hides.

## Verification

- [ ] A test that fails on today's `bootstrap.js` and passes after
- [ ] A mutant covering the transition, caught
- [ ] Re-measured in a real window with Orca: turning the switch off is spoken

## Invariants

- The settle stays: a state that comes back inside `SDT_ANNOUNCE_SETTLE_MS` is
  still not announced, and progress figures are still never spoken.
- Opening the window still announces nothing.

## Exit criteria

Turning indexing off updates the region within the settle, is spoken by a real
screen reader, and a test plus a mutant hold it there.
